gnaux du site","\u002Ffr\u002Fsecurity\u002Fsite-signals","fr\u002F5.security\u002F2.site-signals","i-lucide-globe",{"title":134,"path":135,"stem":136,"icon":137},"Détection web et hôte","\u002Ffr\u002Fsecurity\u002Fdetection","fr\u002F5.security\u002F3.detection","i-lucide-radar",{"title":139,"path":140,"stem":141,"icon":142},"Accès et secrets","\u002Ffr\u002Fsecurity\u002Faccess","fr\u002F5.security\u002F4.access","i-lucide-key-round",{"title":144,"path":145,"stem":146,"icon":147},"Journal et leurres","\u002Ffr\u002Fsecurity\u002Fjournal","fr\u002F5.security\u002F5.journal","i-lucide-book-lock",{"title":149,"path":150,"stem":151,"icon":152},"Conformité et posture","\u002Ffr\u002Fsecurity\u002Fcompliance","fr\u002F5.security\u002F6.compliance","i-lucide-scale",{"title":154,"path":155,"stem":156,"icon":109},"Export SIEM","\u002Ffr\u002Fsecurity\u002Fsiem-export","fr\u002F5.security\u002F7.siem-export",{"title":158,"path":159,"stem":160,"icon":43},"Wazuh et Suricata","\u002Ffr\u002Fsecurity\u002Fwazuh-suricata","fr\u002F5.security\u002F8.wazuh-suricata",{"title":162,"icon":163,"path":164,"stem":165,"children":166,"page":54},"Référence","i-lucide-book-marked","\u002Ffr\u002Freference","fr\u002F6.reference",[167,172,177,182,187],{"title":168,"path":169,"stem":170,"icon":171},"Protocole de l'agent","\u002Ffr\u002Freference\u002Fprotocol","fr\u002F6.reference\u002F1.protocol","i-lucide-arrow-left-right",{"title":173,"path":174,"stem":175,"icon":176},"API de l'UI","\u002Ffr\u002Freference\u002Fui-api","fr\u002F6.reference\u002F2.ui-api","i-lucide-braces",{"title":178,"path":179,"stem":180,"icon":181},"Stockage des métriques","\u002Ffr\u002Freference\u002Fmetric-storage","fr\u002F6.reference\u002F3.metric-storage","i-lucide-database",{"title":183,"path":184,"stem":185,"icon":186},"Performance","\u002Ffr\u002Freference\u002Fperformance","fr\u002F6.reference\u002F4.performance","i-lucide-gauge",{"title":188,"path":189,"stem":190,"icon":191},"Développement","\u002Ffr\u002Freference\u002Fdevelopment","fr\u002F6.reference\u002F5.development","i-lucide-code",{"id":193,"title":10,"body":194,"description":409,"extension":410,"links":411,"meta":412,"navigation":413,"path":6,"seo":414,"stem":7,"__hash__":415},"docs_fr\u002Ffr\u002F1.getting-started\u002F1.index.md",{"type":195,"value":196,"toc":400},"minimark",[197,201,207,212,239,247,251,355,377,381,384,388],[198,199,200],"p",{},"Dodock Wolf est une solution d'observabilité auto-hébergée pour les benches Frappe, les sites\nERPNext et Dokos, et leurs hôtes Linux. Il repère les fenêtres de 502, les crons nocturnes en\néchec, les plantages de workers et les connexions suspectes avant que les clients ne s'en\naperçoivent, et il conserve toutes les données sur un site Frappe que vous exploitez.",[202,203],"screenshot",{"alt":204,"caption":205,"name":206},"La vue d'ensemble de la Wolf UI sur le bench de démonstration","La vue d'ensemble de la Wolf UI après le scénario de 2 h du matin du bench de démonstration.","overview",[208,209,211],"h2",{"id":210},"deux-parties","Deux parties",[213,214,215,230],"card-group",{},[216,217,218],"card",{"icon":33,"title":30,"to":31},[198,219,220,221,225,226,229],{},"Une application Frappe (",[222,223,224],"code",{},"dodock_wolf","). Elle stocke les événements, les métriques, les règles et\nles incidents sous forme de DocTypes, évalue les règles d'alerte à chaque tick du planificateur\net affiche la chronologie dans la Wolf UI sur ",[222,227,228],{},"\u002Fwolf"," et dans Desk.",[216,231,232],{"icon":38,"title":35,"to":36},[198,233,234,235,238],{},"Un démon Python sur chaque hôte, qui n'utilise que la bibliothèque standard (Python 3.9 ou\nultérieur). Il suit les logs nginx, bench et d'authentification, lit ",[222,236,237],{},"\u002Fproc",", Redis, MariaDB et\nles certificats TLS, et envoie des lots en HTTPS.",[198,240,241,242,246],{},"Le site qui exécute la Wolf App se surveille aussi lui-même, sans agent : tâches planifiées en\néchec, Error Logs, connexions échouées, attributions de rôles privilégiés et changements à risque\ncomme de nouveaux Server Scripts. Les autres sites d'un bench peuvent transmettre les mêmes signaux\nen tant que ",[243,244,245],"a",{"href":41},"satellites",".",[208,248,250],{"id":249},"à-quoi-il-sert","À quoi il sert",[252,253,254,270],"table",{},[255,256,257],"thead",{},[258,259,260,264,267],"tr",{},[261,262,263],"th",{},"Signal",[261,265,266],{},"Exemple",[261,268,269],{},"Origine",[271,272,273,289,303,317,334,344],"tbody",{},[258,274,275,279,286],{},[276,277,278],"td",{},"Pics de 5xx et de 502",[276,280,281,282,285],{},"14 × 502 sur ",[222,283,284],{},"a.example.com"," en 5 min, après un déploiement à 01:47",[276,287,288],{},"log d'accès nginx (agent)",[258,290,291,294,297],{},[276,292,293],{},"Échecs de cron et du planificateur",[276,295,296],{},"La tâche nocturne a échoué à 02:00, ou le planificateur s'est bloqué",[276,298,299,302],{},[222,300,301],{},"scheduler.log"," (agent), Scheduled Job Log (site)",[258,304,305,308,311],{},[276,306,307],{},"Problèmes de workers",[276,309,310],{},"Worker tué par l'OOM killer, file d'attente RQ engorgée, aucun worker actif",[276,312,313,316],{},[222,314,315],{},"worker.log",", Redis (agent)",[258,318,319,322,329],{},[276,320,321],{},"Ressources de l'hôte",[276,323,324,325,328],{},"Disque à 93 % sur ",[222,326,327],{},"\u002F",", charge par cœur supérieure à 2",[276,330,331,333],{},[222,332,237],{}," (agent)",[258,335,336,338,341],{},[276,337,121],{},[276,339,340],{},"Force brute SSH, connexion admin depuis un nouveau pays, un scan d'attaque web",[276,342,343],{},"log d'authentification, nginx (agent) ; hooks de connexion et d'audit (site)",[258,345,346,349,352],{},[276,347,348],{},"Exploitation",[276,350,351],{},"Aucune sauvegarde depuis 26 h, certificat TLS qui expire dans 3 jours, réplication arrêtée",[276,353,354],{},"sauvegardes, TLS, MariaDB (agent)",[198,356,357,358,362,363,366,367,370,371,374,375,246],{},"Chaque signal devient un ",[359,360,361],"strong",{},"Wolf Event"," ou un ",[359,364,365],{},"Wolf Metric Sample",". Les ",[359,368,369],{},"Wolf Alert Rules"," les\ntransforment en ",[359,372,373],{},"Wolf Incidents",", qui préviennent vos canaux à leur ouverture, à leur réouverture\net à leur résolution. Voir ",[243,376,18],{"href":19},[208,378,380],{"id":379},"hors-du-périmètre","Hors du périmètre",[198,382,383],{},"Dodock Wolf ne remplace pas entièrement Datadog. Il ne fait ni observabilité des LLM, ni\nobservabilité des données, ni monitoring des utilisateurs réels (RUM), ni tableaux de bord de SLO.\nIl couvre la sûreté opérationnelle de Frappe (erreurs, cron, workers, hôtes) et les signaux de\nsécurité qui l'entourent, avec des formats ouverts (logs JSON, syslog, OCSF) et un stockage qui\nvous appartient.",[208,385,387],{"id":386},"pour-continuer","Pour continuer",[213,389,390,395],{},[216,391,392],{"icon":16,"title":13,"to":14},[198,393,394],{},"De rien à une première alerte, sur un bench.",[216,396,397],{"icon":21,"title":18,"to":19},[198,398,399],{},"Événements, métriques, règles, incidents et périmètres.",{"title":401,"searchDepth":402,"depth":403,"links":404},"",1,2,[405,406,407,408],{"id":210,"depth":403,"text":211},{"id":249,"depth":403,"text":250},{"id":379,"depth":403,"text":380},{"id":386,"depth":403,"text":387},"Ce qu'est Dodock Wolf, ce qu'il surveille et comment ses deux parties s'articulent.","md",null,{},{"icon":11},{"title":10,"description":409},"EYbYWY9qiuCxtfghCFmxfxPENI03fEWIsyvxXgwCt1w",[411,417],{"title":13,"path":14,"stem":15,"description":418,"icon":16},"Installez la Wolf App, placez un agent sur l'hôte et obtenez une première alerte, sur un bench.",1795042368301]